WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.800
The Riemann Hypothesis

00:00:01.612 --> 00:00:02.625
proof checks out

00:00:02.437 --> 00:00:03.133
in Lean

00:00:03.654 --> 00:00:05.128
On November 20

00:00:05.199 --> 00:00:06.767
Levent Alpöge released

00:00:06.579 --> 00:00:07.392
a proof of

00:00:07.204 --> 00:00:08.665
the Riemann Hypothesis

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:09.361
as a Lean

00:00:09.173 --> 00:00:10.847
library with 17

00:00:10.659 --> 00:00:11.602
million lines of

00:00:11.413 --> 00:00:11.979
code

00:00:12.133 --> 00:00:13.429
depending only on

00:00:13.241 --> 00:00:14.078
Mathlib

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:15.557
Within a day

00:00:15.664 --> 00:00:16.630
dozens of people

00:00:16.442 --> 00:00:17.455
compiled it and

00:00:17.338 --> 00:00:18.611
reproduced the same

00:00:18.423 --> 00:00:19.555
raw proof export

00:00:19.673 --> 00:00:20.958
and two independent

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:21.854
tools confirmed it

00:00:21.666 --> 00:00:23.246
proves exactly Mathlib's

00:00:23.057 --> 00:00:23.788
statement

00:00:24.326 --> 00:00:25.717
Several proof checkers

00:00:25.647 --> 00:00:26.849
including formally

00:00:26.661 --> 00:00:27.745
verified ones

00:00:27.828 --> 00:00:28.677
accepted it

00:00:28.701 --> 00:00:29.550
and the Lean

00:00:29.361 --> 00:00:30.835
and Mathlib communities

00:00:30.647 --> 00:00:31.731
now certify the

00:00:31.543 --> 00:00:32.757
proof as correct

00:00:33.294 --> 00:00:34.308
Full story on

00:00:34.119 --> 00:00:35.015
the dashboard
